{"created": "2026-10-13T05:49:11.621031+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-13T05:49:13.546664+00:00", "id": 23333002, "conceptrecid": "23333001", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23333002", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23333001", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23333002", "metadata": {"title": "A Robinson counterexample to ideal-only tangency certificates", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23333002", "publication_date": "2026-10-12", "description": "<p>The classical Robinson sextic is globally nonnegative, but adding any nonnegative constant does not make it a finite sum of real polynomial squares modulo even the full ideal of polynomials vanishing on its real tangency variety. This refutes both the exact ordinary-radical certificate and the every-positive-epsilon original-ideal certificate proposed in the unrestricted tangency-minor formulation of Schweighofer's 2007 question. The same zero-line and coordinate-axis obstruction refutes the separate-cross-product reading printed in the report. Arbitrarily many summands of arbitrary degree are allowed. The attained example is within the unrestricted question; a separate nonattaining diagnostic concerns only the literal-product reading and uses a constant shift of the standard example in Schweighofer (2006), Section 1.6, equation (6). The standard sphere-minimization mechanism retains its attribution to Laurent's updated manuscript dated 6 February 2010, Section 7.2.3, Lemma 7.21, manuscript pages 117-118 (https://homepages.cwi.nl/~monique/files/moment-ima-update-new.pdf). The earlier 2009 published chapter has a different Lemma 7.21; its DOI is bibliographic context, not the tangency locator. Robinson's form and classical zero-set ingredients retain their attribution. The identical ten-zero cubic obstruction is explicitly credited to Reznick (2000), Section 4(b), printed page 259, authenticated in the author-hosted publisher reprint. Complete 2008 and 2009 Ha-Pham article texts were not obtained; truncated-certificate comparisons rely on later primary statements and the access gaps remain disclosed. The 66-record citation graph is a metadata screen with marked primary-text follow-ups. No author-approved formula correction, first bibliographic priority or continued open status through 2026 is asserted.</p><p>This unrefereed research note is accompanied by its unchanged historical candidate, reproducible exact-algebra checks, fresh independent adversarial proof/computational/source reviews, and a bounded priority audit. AI tools were used extensively in development, verification, adversarial review and writing. Independent AI-assisted review is not independent human or journal peer review; the note has received neither. Finite controls supplement the universal mathematical proof and are not formal proof-assistant certification or numerical SOS-degree-cutoff evidence.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["sums of squares", "Robinson sextic", "tangency variety", "polynomial nonnegativity", "real algebraic geometry", "gradient ideal", "counterexample", "Oberwolfach Report 14/2007", "reproducible exact verification"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/905", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.4171/owr/2007/14", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1137/050647098", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1137/080719212", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://perso.lip6.fr/Mohab.Safey/Articles/gcv_sos.pdf", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1090/conm/253/03936", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/978-0-387-09686-5_7", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://homepages.cwi.nl/~monique/files/moment-ima-update-new.pdf", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0", "references": ["Markus Schweighofer, Gradient tentacles and sums of squares, Oberwolfach Report 14/2007, pp.810ff., Conjecture 2 p.811, DOI 10.4171/owr/2007/14.", "Bruce Reznick, Hilbert's construction of psd polynomials that are not a sum of squares, Oberwolfach Report 14/2007, pp.797-799, Robinson form p.798 equation (2), DOI 10.4171/owr/2007/14.", "Markus Schweighofer, Global optimization of polynomials using gradient tentacles and sums of squares, SIAM J. Optim. 17(3) (2006),920-942, DOI 10.1137/050647098.", "Ha Huy Vui and Pham Tien Son, Global optimization of polynomials using the truncated tangency variety and sums of squares, SIAM J. Optim. 19(2) (2008),941-951, DOI 10.1137/080719212.", "Feng Guo, Mohab Safey El Din and Lihong Zhi, Global optimization of polynomials using generalized critical values and sums of squares, ISSAC 2010, author manuscript https://perso.lip6.fr/Mohab.Safey/Articles/gcv_sos.pdf.", "Bruce Reznick, Some concrete aspects of Hilbert's 17th problem, Contemporary Mathematics 253 (2000), 251-272, DOI 10.1090/conm/253/03936; Section 4(b), printed p.259. Author-hosted publisher reprint https://reznick.web.illinois.edu/Paper34.pdf.", "Monique Laurent, Sums of squares, moment matrices and optimization over polynomials, updated manuscript, 6 February 2010, Section 7.2.3, Lemma 7.21, manuscript pp.117-118, https://homepages.cwi.nl/~monique/files/moment-ima-update-new.pdf. Earlier published chapter in Emerging Applications of Algebraic Geometry, IMA Volumes 149, Springer (2009),157-270, DOI 10.1007/978-0-387-09686-5_7; that published Lemma 7.21 is not the cited tangency lemma."], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23333001"}}]}}, "title": "A Robinson counterexample to ideal-only tangency certificates", "link